WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.810
Today, I'm going to
talk about my latest

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:10.210
project, the Dashboard
Builder, or how

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.610
to build Shiny apps
without writing code.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:15.470
Now quick disclaimer.

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:17.510
This is not the UI Builder.

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:19.330
So yesterday at
the keynote, it was

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.520
a bit of an emotional
roller coaster for me

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.530
because I saw, oh, you
guys are doing UI builder,

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:24.738
I'm doing a dashboard builder.

00:00:24.738 --> 00:00:27.650
OK, I'm just going to
see myself out, OK?

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:31.800
Nothing to do here. But I think
it's still a bit different.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.370
So if I'm not from
RStudio, then who am I?

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:37.020
Well, I'm Peter.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:40.410
I just finished my masters in
data engineering and analytics

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:43.650
from the Technical
University in Munich.

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:46.500
And in my free time,
I like to play chess

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:50.640
and do data visualizations,
especially Shiny dashboards.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.670
Now, when I talk to people and
tell them about my hobbies,

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.320
well, most call me a nerd.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.530
But there are also a
few people who say,

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:00.460
oh, visualizations, dashboards.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.820
I would like to create
more dashboards,

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:06.090
but I don't know how.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:08.020
It's I can't write R code.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:09.570
It's too complex.

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:13.180
And then there are some
people who say, I could do it.

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:14.170
I know how to do it.

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:16.120
But I have so many great ideas.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:18.820
I just don't have enough time.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:20.950
And I think these are
all valid reasons.

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:21.920
But I'm here.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:25.180
I want to tell you to
create more dashboards.

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:28.570
So more dashboards
like this one I

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:31.600
created about my
recent chess games.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:33.430
Is this the most
sophisticated,

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:35.730
the most beautiful
dashboard you've ever seen?

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:36.550
Probably not.

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:37.380
I hope not.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.740
If it is, go check
out the Shiny gallery.

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:42.790
Go check out some
Shiny contests.

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:45.850
But I still think that
that's a decent dashboard.

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:49.720
And everyone in this room
can build this dashboard

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:53.260
without writing R code,
without prior knowledge

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:54.140
of Shiny.

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:59.780
And you can do it in two
minutes and 22 seconds.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:02.690
I know, but I can
prove it to you.

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:05.810
I have a video and you can
see the time on the bottom.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:09.470
Right so if you open
up the Dashboard Builder,

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:11.360
you've created with
a blank screen.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:14.630
And if you want to visualize
data, well, you need data.

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:18.980
So I downloaded some of my chess
games, saved it as a CSV file,

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:22.280
and then I'm just loading it
into the Dashboard Builder.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:26.510
And then I could add elements
like a table about the date

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:28.160
and the results of my games.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:31.460
And then I'm adding a graph
about my rating points.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:34.940
So in chess, if you win
games, you gain rating points.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:37.070
If you lose, you
lose rating points.

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:38.690
So I can visualize this.

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:41.420
I can add some value
boxes about the number

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:42.950
of games I've played.

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:44.390
The number is too high.

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:48.340
And my peak rating.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:50.650
And then I can
add more elements.

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:53.260
And if it's too small for you,
if you can't see everything

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:55.190
that's going on, that's fine.

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:58.720
I just want to take
away how easy it is.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.230
You don't have to
write any code.

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:03.560
And trust me, it's
also a lot of fun.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:08.450
And while I'm here creating
the last couple of graphs,

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:10.430
the next part is the
interesting part.

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:12.740
There is an export
button up there

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:15.490
and once you click on Export,
the Dashboard Builder

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:17.390
generates R code.

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:22.390
It generates the R code that is
needed to build this dashboard.

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.760
And then it downloads this.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:30.270
And then you can open
it up in RStudio.

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.560
And then.

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:34.190
You open up the file.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:35.145
And once you hit, run.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:45.560
Now look, it looks exactly
like the one we just created.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:47.900
OK so now you have a
first impression of what

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:49.760
the Dashboard Builder can do.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:52.550
So I quickly want to
say what it is not.

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:55.520
So it's not a standalone tool.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:04:00.200
It's not Power BI, Tableau,
or whatever in R.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.310
Why not?

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:03.950
I think these tools
are great, but there

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:05.690
are certain soft locks.

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:09.830
I think with every tool
you have the ease of use

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:12.830
versus the extendability
and power.

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:15.500
Now, this part is
highly opinionated,

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:17.360
so please don't be angry.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:21.329
I think Power BI is easy to
use, but it's not powerful.

00:04:21.329 --> 00:04:24.980
You can't do machine learning,
deep learning, serious data

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:29.380
science, or if you want
to do it, it's very hard.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:32.200
And then let's look at
R. If you combine it

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:36.740
with HTML, JavaScript and
CSS, it's super powerful.

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:40.630
We all know what R can
do, but I would argue

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:42.220
it's not that easy to use.

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:43.570
So what can we do?

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:48.370
Well, we can use R and Shiny,
which is a bit easier to use,

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:51.250
but I still think there's
something up there

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.700
and I want to go up there.

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:54.840
What's up there?

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:59.610
Well, I think up there
is a WYSIWYG dashboard

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:02.280
builder. WYSIWYG means what
you see is what you get.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:04.860
So if you have
R Markdown, that's not

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:06.860
WYSIWYG because you
have to build it.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:09.720
So if you want to increase the
size of a picture in markdown,

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:13.118
you have to put in
width 50%, width 70%,

00:05:13.118 --> 00:05:14.910
and then you build it
and then you can see,

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:17.243
oh, it's too small, so you
have to get back to the code.

00:05:17.243 --> 00:05:20.640
If you compare this to
Powerpoint, which is WYSIWYG,

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.680
if you want to increase
the size of an image,

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.970
you click on the image
and you scale it.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.487
And then that's how big it is.

00:05:26.487 --> 00:05:27.320
That's what you get.

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:30.210
What you see is what you get.

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:34.620
But I also want all the
power and packages of R.

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:36.390
I want the data science.

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:37.890
I want the machine learning.

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:40.140
I want the visualizations.

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:42.580
So that's what I want.

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:44.720
A combination of these.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:46.850
So why?

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:47.850
What does it add?

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:49.100
Who is it for?

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:51.230
And I think there are
two target groups.

00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:53.480
The first one, beginners.

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:55.490
I don't think that
only data scientists

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:56.930
should create dashboards.

00:05:56.930 --> 00:05:58.280
There are other sciences.

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:01.400
They have so much data,
so much insight that they

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:04.550
can use to create dashboards.

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:06.800
But it has to be easy to
use, because most of them

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:08.330
don't know how to write code.

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:11.810
And I think the
blank screen, when

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:14.020
you start a project,
that's really frightening.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:16.970
So if we can help
them first step

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:19.850
without them having to
know how to program,

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:21.980
I think that's going
to lower the entry

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:24.870
barrier to data visualization.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:26.460
And then there are the experts.

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:30.750
But if you just go to a client
discuss how the dashboard will

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:32.400
look like, that's
never going to be how

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:34.110
it will look like in the end.

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:36.900
So you create the
dashboard, then

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:38.040
you bring it to the client

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.850
who tells you, how
can we change this?

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:42.340
So you have to go back,
change it, go to the client.

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:43.200
Can we change this?

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:46.740
No. I want you to be there
in the room with a client

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:50.460
or maybe just with your team,
and build a rapid prototype,

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:52.110
build the dashboard.

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:55.120
So we're going to streamline
the dashboard building process.

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:59.860
So you have more time for
the really interesting stuff.

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:04.270
So now you're wondering,
how does it work?

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:06.160
If you open it up,
there are three buttons

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:09.190
and these three buttons are the
three steps you have to take.

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:10.642
You have to import data.

00:07:10.642 --> 00:07:12.350
Then you're going to
build the dashboard.

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:13.600
And then you export it.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:16.870
And then there's a
fourth open ended step,

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:19.040
improve and extend.

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:22.140
So we're going to import data.

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:26.340
With this module up
here, we can import data

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:27.990
from our R environment.

00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:31.290
We can load external
files and Google Sheets.

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:33.340
Now, I did not create this.

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:36.370
I shamelessly stole it from
the guys from dreamRs.

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:37.200
DreamRs?

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:39.230
Yeah.

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:41.240
And once you've
loaded the data, you

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:43.740
can start to build
the dashboard.

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:45.070
Now there are two steps.

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:47.010
First, you create the element.

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:51.180
Right now, we support text
boxes, value boxes, data tables

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:53.170
and graphs.

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:56.290
So for text boxes,
just put in the text

00:07:56.290 --> 00:07:59.260
you want to be displayed.
For value boxes, put

00:07:59.260 --> 00:08:03.420
in a title, the value
and then an icon.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.280
Data tables? Also very easy.

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:09.320
Just select the columns
you want to be displayed.

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:13.100
But how are we going
to create ggplots,

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:15.800
graphs without writing code?

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:18.710
And thankfully, the
guys from dreamRs

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:20.760
have this awesome
esquisse package.

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:23.300
I'm sure most of
you have seen it.

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:27.320
You see up there in the top,
those are all your columns

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:30.560
from your data, and then you
can drag and drop these columns

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:34.190
and to the x, the
y, maybe the color,

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:39.620
whatever, and then it's going
to create a graph for you.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:41.990
And then you have this element.

00:08:41.990 --> 00:08:44.330
And then you can.

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:46.260
Edit the content.

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:47.530
You can scale it.

00:08:47.530 --> 00:08:49.210
You can move it around.

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:53.130
And you can also delete it.
And then just kind of repeat

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:54.300
these two steps.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:58.350
So add an element, scale,
it, add an element,

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:01.920
scale it, add more
elements, move them around,

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:05.010
and then you kind of
build your dashboard.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:09.000
And as soon as you're happy
with how it looks, export it.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:10.890
And when you export
it, you get three files

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:12.900
you get the R project.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:16.350
You get that data that
you loaded in as an Rds file,

00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:19.020
and you get the app.R file.

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:23.490
And in the app there's
always a UI and a server.

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:26.520
And now let's look a bit deeper
into the UI and the server

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:27.140
files.

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:29.400
Let's start with the UI
for these two elements,

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:34.500
two value boxes. Internally, we
use the grid stacker package.

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:39.300
So we just add a grid stack item,
give it a height, a width, x y,

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:42.360
give it some ID, some
styling, and then in there,

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:45.540
please give us a
value box output.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:48.430
Now we're going to do the
same for the second one.

00:09:48.430 --> 00:09:50.310
And if that looks
a bit complicated,

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:52.080
if it was too fast, don't worry.

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:55.950
All of this is 100% generated
by the Dashboard Builder

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:58.560
and we also have the
same for server.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:00.550
We're going to
render a value box.

00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:01.660
Which value box?

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:06.150
Well, just this title games
played, the value is 200

00:10:06.150 --> 00:10:08.250
and then we have
an icon and a width

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:13.200
and the same for the second
one. And again 100% generated.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:16.040
But now comes to the
part where I have

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:17.840
to admit that I lied to you.

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:20.540
You do have to write
a tiny bit of code

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:22.670
because, look, the
value of boxes,

00:10:22.670 --> 00:10:24.560
the values are hard coded.

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:28.580
So if the data changes, these
values will stay the same.

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:31.520
And that brings us to
the fourth and final step,

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:33.560
to improve and extend.

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:35.660
Now that you have
your dashboard,

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:38.030
you can do so much with it.

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:42.290
And in our case, let's
see, games played.

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:45.500
That's just the number
of rows of my data table.

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:48.050
And the highest rating? Well
the highest rating is just

00:10:48.050 --> 00:10:49.700
the max of my rating.

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:53.600
So you have to write these
two tiny lines of code.

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:57.590
And I think most of us, most
of you, all of you, all of you

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:58.580
can do that.

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:01.950
And then when you've done
that, you get your dashboard.

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:06.770
Now I know what
you all want to do.

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:08.410
You want to use the
Dashboard Builder.

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:11.050
It's still in
alpha, but it works.

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:13.960
So you can get a
demo on Shiny apps.

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:15.510
You can go to my GitHub.

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:18.550
That will bring
you to my GitHub.

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:22.800
But you need for
both for the GitHub

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:24.280
if you want to run it locally.

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:26.820
And if you want to run
the apps that you created,

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:29.280
you need the grid
stacker package and you

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:31.350
can download this from GitHub.

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:33.630
I'm going to put it
on CRAN, but right now

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:37.510
you still have to do the
devtools install GitHub.

00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:41.380
And then how can we all
improve the Dashboard Builder?

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:44.290
Well, I was a bit busy
in the last two months

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:46.180
because I had to finish
my master's thesis,

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:48.980
but now I have some free time.

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:51.850
I'm just job hunting, and I
want to improve the Dashboard Builder.

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:54.820
So please, if you have
feedback, if you have ideas,

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:57.110
if you have questions,
write me an email.

00:11:57.110 --> 00:12:00.340
Open up an issue on GitHub
or just ask me right now.

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:02.160
Thank you.

